had a son named  forrest mars in 1904  unfortunately the two would divorce soon  after but what's funny is that frank  would go ahead and marry another woman  named ethel in 1910  one year later frank and itahini would  start the mars candy company together in  tacoma washington  the company specialized in wholesaling  fresh candy but they weren't the only  company in the area targeting this  market a company called brown and haley  came around just a few years later and  they would prove to be a lot more  successful  frank and ethel had a daughter named  patricia in 1914 and they tried to keep  up with the mars candy company as long  as they could  but eventually they threw in the towel  and moved to minneapolis minnesota in  1920.  in minneapolis the duo started a new  chocolate company called the marzo bar  that manufactured chocolate bars  in 1923 frank introduced a new chocolate  bar based on a sunforest idea called the  milky way bar  milky way became a customer favorite and  propelled the business into being an  up-and-coming chocolate company several  years later in 1929 frank would move to  chicago where he would come up with the  snickers bar  things were finally starting to pick up  and frank would start to enjoy himself  in the late 1920s frank started  construction on a massive estate called  the milky way farm  the estate consisted of a 25 000 square  feet clubhouse over 30 barns and it even  had a horse racing track  apparently frank employed 935 men to  construct the estate  but just as the estate was completed  frank would pass away at age 50 in 1934  due to heart problems  unfortunately it looks like enjoying his  walls just wasn't in the cards with the  frank dead the responsibility of running  the company naturally fell on his kids  but his son forest had already gone on  his own path  given that frank and his first wife etho  had divorced soon after forrest's birth  forest wasn't that close with his father  forrest and his mother had moved to  canada after the divorce and forrest  rarely saw his father  forest ended up attending the university  of california berkeley before  transferring to yale and graduating with  an industrial engineering degree in 1928  after graduation forest did join his  father's company but he didn't stick  around for too long at first forrest  oversaw the development of the snickers  and three musketeers bars but soon  enough forrest wanted to expand the  company internationally however frank  had no interest in expanding  internationally eventually the argument  would blow over and force ended up  moving to england alone in england  forest took on jobs at nestle and the  tobler company but he never let go of  his chocolate roots either in the  background forest was developing the  mars bar and mount teasers in 1934  forest bought a british company called  chapel bros which produced canned dog  food there was very little competition  in the market so it wasn't that hard for  forest dominate the dog food market but  after his father's death forest would  move back to the u.s  forest did oversee his father's company  but he wouldn't take over the company  for quite some time his stepmom ito  healey became the president of mars inc  and she was in charge of day-to-day  operations  in the meantime forest created his own  food business called food manufacturers  i think we can all agree that that's  literally the lamest name he could have  given the business  despite the lame name the company would  go on to be quite successful under food  manufacturers forest started two  sub-brands called uncle ben's rice and  pedigree the famous pet food brand  forrest kept coming up with new product  ideas from mars as well  in 1940 forrest came up with the idea  for m ms the idea was to create a  chocolate that didn't melt in your hands  but would melt in your mouth  given that this was during world war ii  though forest was worried that sugar and  chocolate would be rationed  so forest formed a partnership with the  president of hershey william murray  this way the two companies could share  resources if rationing wasn't forced  this is also how the name for eminem  came about the name was indicative of  the partnership between mars and the  murray ironically these companies are  massive rivals today  anyway a few years later in 1945 four's  stepmom passed away and this gave  forrest and his stepsister patricia the  full responsibility of running the  company in 1954 forrest introduced  peanut m ms and fun fact forest was  actually extremely allergic to peanuts  forest continued to run his father's  company and his own company separately  for another 10 years but finally in 1964  30 years after his father's death forest  merged the two companies  it's not clear what exactly happened to  patricia's stake in the business or if  she even had one patricia died just one  year later in 1965 and it doesn't look  like she had any kids so maybe forrest  inherited her steak after her death or  maybe he bought other steak while she  was still alive whatever the case though  forest was left with the entire business  given forrest's massive influence in the  company starting with the milky way bar  way back in 1923 i think this is only  fitting over the next decade forest  continued to run the company with a  tight fist forrest was notorious for  having an extreme temper and he highly  valued punctuality and performance  forced incentivize these traits by  offering a 10 bonus to all mars  employees  if the company was hitting performance  metrics and you were on time the entire  week you got a 10 bonus that week but if  you were late even once you  automatically lost a bonus regardless of  whether you're a janitor or an executive  forrest officially retired in 1973 and  age 69 but he had quite a bit of trouble  actually letting go  he left the company with his three  children forest junior john and  jacqueline  apparently he would call his kids all  the time to nitpick at things that they  weren't doing quite right but eventually  for forest senior lightened up on his  kids after he founded a new chocolate  company to run in 1981 forrest senior  moved to henderson nevada and founded  ethel am chocolates he ran the company  for seven years but in 1988 he would  sell the company to mars inc and truly  retire  ford's senior ended up passing away in  1998 at age 95 after living a stunning  life as for more zinc the company only  grew even larger under the leadership of  forest kids  after forest senior left the company the  kids move their headquarters to mclean  virginia the company is super famous for  being secretive so we don't know too  much about their internal operations or  business decisions but one avenue of  growth that we are aware of is their  public acquisitions and the kids haven't  been shy when it comes to acquisitions  they bought the chewing gum company  wrigley jr in 2008 for 23 billion  dollars  similarly they bought three pet food  brands from png for 2.9 billion dollars  in 2014. they also expanded into new  areas through acquisitions  for example in 2003 mars acquired  aquarium pharmaceuticals which allowed  the company to enter the aquarium and  bond markets  similarly they bought banfield pet  hospital in 2007.  since then morris has doubled down on  the veterinary market mars went ahead  and bought blueprint veterinary partners  in 2015 vca inc in 2017 and the lineage  group in 2018. all of these acquisitions  have actually made mars the largest pet  nutrition and veterinary care provider  in the world today the kids aren't  really kids anymore as they're in their  80s and forest junior actually passed  away in 2016. his take in the company  was evenly split between his four  children who all work at mars as well  as for john mars he has three kids but  we don't know what exactly they do and  if they're even involved with the  company john himself has chosen to live  an extremely private and peaceful life  in wyoming in fact he's kept his life so  private that when forbes was making  their billionaires list from 2010 to  2014 they couldn't find a picture of him  which made him the richest person on the  list without a picture  and finally we have jacqueline who is  likely the most public of the three  we don't know too much about her three  children either but in 2013 jacqueline  was involved in an infamous car accident  near her house  jacqueline claims that she passed out  while driving but she tested negative  for drugs alcohol and medication  so it's not clear what exactly caused a  blackout  but unfortunately the accident resulted  in a person dying and a pregnant woman  miscarrying jacqueline pleaded guilty  and profusely apologized for the  incident  fortunately for jacqueline she was  eventually able to walk away from the  situation with a misdemeanor charge for  reckless driving and that's the story of  the 141 billion chocolate family did you  guys know about the mars family comment  that down below also drop a like if you  love snickers  and of course consider joining our  discord community to suggest future  video ideas and consider subscribing to  see more questions logically answered  but until then i'm ari and i'll see you  guys on the next one  you
 

